{
 "title": "Blood Squirt",
 "summary": "A blood squirt. The tutor simulates it with Quick Liquid (a stretched icosphere emitter with initial velocity, a flat collider in front, two side emitters shooting inward, a baked domain meshed with a small particle radius); the fluid solver can't run in this headless build, so the same set-up is made with emitter particles (initial velocity, gravity) rendered as metaballs that melt into liquid where they touch, colliding with the flat plate. The tutor's blood shader: a fresnel edge mask mixing a dark inside and a brighter red rim, glossy highlights through Shader to RGB and a constant ramp, and a second fresnel ramp keyed so the blood grows in and shrinks away from the edges (Blended).",
 "objects": [
  {
   "name": "Squirt",
   "description": "the main emitter"
  },
  {
   "name": "Drop",
   "description": "the metaball"
  }
 ],
